      ],
      "assessment": "The first block writes the same six-row design, zeros only the last six state parameters, solves the same first-epoch 6x6 map against target minus nuisance-evaluated state, and uses the solved global parameter vector for every block. Full evaluated position/velocity arrays are assembled before the byte-identical original interpolation tail. Pulse velocity uses right-side selection at exact boundaries and omits post-pulse endpoints from preceding interpolation stencils; density boundaries remain continuous. No interpolation occurs separately within storage blocks.",
      "topic": "Initial state and interpolation"
    },
    {
