        "native-source-01/source/base/matrix.h:714",
        "native-source-01/source/base/matrix.cpp:852"
      ],
      "assessment": "Two design matrices are 3B by P, plus per-epoch 3 by P temporaries and the native O(P) accumulator/integrand machinery. Only two 3N by 1 evaluated arrays escape the loop. Native Matrix copies separate MatrixBase handles but share the data pointer until field() detaches on write, so matMult does not corrupt equation.pos0/vel0 during reanchoring. copy into result rows copies values and retains no design slice. Block equation and evaluated temporaries leave scope before the next integrateArc allocation. The claim is bounded design-row storage, not constant total memory; the full propagation archive, evaluated trajectory and original native event data remain resident.",
      "topic": "Allocation, ownership and copy-on-write"
    },
